            { "ui.buttonTooltip", "Transit Timetables" },
            { "ui.panelTitle", "ARRIVALS" },
            { "ui.panelHint", "Select a stop to see how often each line comes and when it is next expected. To change a line's vehicle counts, select the line — its controls are in the line's info panel." },
            { "opt.VehicleCounts.L", "Vehicle count" },
            { "opt.VehicleCounts.D", "Who decides how many vehicles each timetabled line runs. \"Let the mod decide\" (recommended) sizes every line by measuring how long its route really takes, so it can actually hold the interval you set, and needs no attention. In this mode the mod owns the count on every timetabled line: the game's own Assigned Vehicles slider will not stick, because the mod re-applies its own number. \"Do not let the mod decide\" hands every line back and never touches counts again, so you or a dedicated fleet mod can own them. Departure holds work exactly the same either way. If a line asks for more vehicles than you want, widen its interval; that is the real control." },
            { "ui.noticeTitle", "Transit Timetables now works by vehicle count" },
            { "ui.noticeBody", "Until now you told this mod how often a line should run and it worked out how many vehicles that needed. It is the other way round now: you say how many vehicles run in the peak, off-peak and at night, and the mod keeps them evenly spaced by holding them a little longer at the terminus." },
