            { "opt.MinTerminusDwell.L", "Minimum layover at a terminus (minutes)" },
            { "opt.MinTerminusDwell.D", "How long a vehicle stands at its terminus before setting off again, even when it is exactly on its interval. This is the line's recovery time: without it a vehicle that loses two minutes in traffic can never win them back, every vehicle behind it inherits the delay, and the line drifts permanently. Real operators build a few minutes of standing time into every turn for exactly this reason. The cost is that this time is part of the round trip and so part of the interval — with 10 vehicles, 2 minutes here widens the interval by 12 seconds; on a 2-vehicle shuttle it widens it by a full minute. Set it to 0 only if you want vehicles to turn round instantly and accept that the line can never recover from a delay. A Terminus B, if you set one, has its own minimum on the stop panel and both are counted. Default 2 minutes." },
